  "reason": "With only 2 completed experiments (both using scgpt + imagenet_vit_l), the evidence is too sparse to confidently exploit one direction. The most critical unresolved question is whether the RNA encoder choice (scgpt vs scvi_n200) materially affects performance. config_020 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat, multiprofile) is a clean single-variable comparison against the current best (config_014: scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat, multiprofile), isolating the RNA encoder while holding image encoder, aggregation, fusion, and profile setting constant. If scvi_n200 matches or beats scgpt, it opens a large sub-space of configurations for the remaining 7 experiments; if scgpt is clearly superior, I can confidently focus the budget on the scgpt+imagenet_vit_l region. This reduces the most impactful uncertainty with a direct, interpretable comparison."
}

